PySlope
-------
This product vendors source files from PySlope (1.4.0), a 2D slope
stability library, executed in-browser via Pyodide.

  Homepage:  https://github.com/JesseBonanno/PySlope
  License:   MIT
  Copyright (c) 2022, Jesse Bonanno

Vendored files (src/lib/calculations/geotech/vendor/pyslope/):
  data_validation.py, utilities.py  — unmodified
  pyslope.py                        — patched (see pyslope.manifest.json)
  __init__.py                       — patched (see pyslope.manifest.json)

Vendor tree SHA-256: d5b91642583cd46bd4a9d7a4ba88e569f0b66d1f30fcf85bf781d3a50a2d2374

The plotting paths (plotly/tqdm/colour) are never executed: Concreta consumes
only the numeric results and renders its own SVG. Those imports are satisfied by
lightweight stubs at runtime (numpy-only). The full MIT license text is preserved
in vendor/pyslope/LICENSE.txt.

Seismic hazard table (NCSE-02, Anejo 1)
---------------------------------------
This product redistributes the seismic hazard values (basic seismic
acceleration ab and contribution coefficient K, per municipality) published by
the Instituto Geográfico Nacional as the INSPIRE layer HazardArea2002.NCSE-02.

  Source:       https://www.ign.es/wms-inspire/geofisica
  Layer:        HazardArea2002.NCSE-02
  License:      CC BY 4.0 ign.es
  License text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Attribution:  Instituto Geográfico Nacional (IGN)

The bulk of the table (2,610 of 2,635 rows) is harvested from that layer by
scripts/harvest-ign-hazard.mjs. The remaining rows, and one corrected value,
do not come from the layer — they are transcribed from the legal text itself
and from the official municipal register:

  Legal text:   Real Decreto 997/2002, Anejo 1
                BOE núm. 244, 11/10/2002, pages 35949-35967
                https://www.boe.es/boe/dias/2002/10/11/pdfs/A35898-35967.pdf
                (Spanish law; official texts are not subject to copyright —
                Ley de Propiedad Intelectual, art. 13)
  Municipal register (INE), used only for 5-digit municipality codes and for
  the list of municipalities created after 2002:
                https://www.ine.es/daco/daco42/codmun/codmun_anual.htm
                Reuse permitted under the INE's terms, attribution required.
                Attribution: Instituto Nacional de Estadística (INE)

Generated files (src/features/seismic-ncse02/):
  ncse02.hazard.json           — table, columnar form, with a per-row
                                 provenance map for the supplemented rows
  ncse02.hazard.manifest.json  — provenance, license, SHA-256, record counts

Only municipalities listed in Anejo 1 of NCSE-02 are kept; those the layer
publishes with a null acceleration are outside Anejo 1 (ab < 0.04 g) and are
counted in the manifest but not shipped. See scripts/ncse02-suplemento.mjs for
why six municipalities — Ceuta and Melilla among them — are read from the BOE
rather than from the layer, and how municipalities created after 2002 inherit
from the term they were split from.
